id: pm-htiwmd
title: Replace unsafe live-lock force advice with invocation-preserving contention recovery
description: "Bounded delivery of the recovery-guidance defect reported in GH-1516: live or unknown locks must recommend waiting and the actual command, never placeholder item updates or force takeover. Keep the thousand-writer throughput and hierarchy-lock redesign in canonical parent pm-lvyd."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,concurrency,recovery
created_at: "2026-10-20T15:15:31.532Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T16:56:55.490Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-20T16:56:52.605Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-20T16:56:52.605Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Human and JSON recovery preserve actual command arguments and item identity; no live-lock force advice or placeholder mutation; SDK conflict context exposes owner liveness and wait policy; shell-sensitive operands stay quoted; tests prove original payload and lock survive refusals
parent: pm-lvyd
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Replace placeholder force advice with actual normalized retry commands, observed owner-process state and bounded wait guidance. Preserve padded/empty arguments, reject malformed vectors whole, retain portable quoting and document actual TTL semantics."
expected_result: "Contending callers retain their exact operation and argument values, receive truthful wait/liveness guidance and avoid invented force mutations on unexpired live or unknown locks."
actual_result: "Native diagnostic and real CLI controls pass, including malformed vectors and padded/empty operands.197 focused review tests and final linked commands pass; exact-head CI is green with all four source coverage metrics100percent. Requested review fixes are resolved; provider quota limitations are explicit and final closure revision awaits review before merge."
