comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T15:15:31.532Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: fresh context/search/open/in-progress and complete strict all-status corpus (3027 items without omissions), plus full pm-lvyd/pm-02z97f and completed retry/takeover/publication/GC lineage reads. No active leaf owns the precise live-lock guidance defect. This child implements only recovery guidance; large-scale throughput remains with pm-lvyd."
  "2026-10-20T15:26:15.655Z","harness:codex","Implemented invocation-preserving recovery on the shared CLI error surface, using already-redacted normalized argv from the runtime. SDK conflicts include actual lock id, observed owner-liveness reason, bounded-wait recovery policy and retry hint. Live or unknown locks receive wait/configuration advice rather than invented force mutations. Shell-sensitive comment operands survive tokenized recovery. Focused aggregate: 238 passing tests; full gates pending."
  "2026-10-20T15:53:29.971Z","harness:codex","Follow-up acceptance:57 tests across the moved lock journey, owner-proof boundaries and all three previous failing suites now pass. Real packed SDK continuation acceptance succeeds under both Node and Bun after qualifying the local npm resolution environment. The repository file cap remains120 and the suppression ceiling is lowered to103. Full static and terminal coverage checks are pending; no full-coverage success is claimed from the earlier run."
  "2026-10-20T15:59:29.776Z","harness:codex","Investigation while the static gate runs: the shared recovery normalizer trims opaque argv entries and drops empty tokens. A retry can therefore change a whitespace-sensitive payload even when the lock guidance retains the original command. This is inside this leaf's argument-preservation acceptance: preserve complete validated token arrays and add padded/empty operand controls, alongside a native SDK owner-state and live-lock protection assertion. No new duplicate issue is needed."
  "2026-10-20T16:07:46.879Z","harness:codex","Argument-preservation acceptance passes: validated normalized and suggested retry vectors preserve padded and empty operands exactly. Invalid vectors are omitted whole rather than dropping tokens. Live conflicts report observed owner-process state and actual lock identity, and safe retries retain canonical command, operands and shell quoting without adding force. Final focused aggregate240 tests passes, including direct public diagnostic and real CLI transport controls."
  "2026-10-20T16:12:20.638Z","harness:codex","Combined implementation PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1523 at13d89b48f. Same-head checks and all installed external reviewers requested once; remaining source findings will be handled within this PR. Final package-generated changelog and closure evidence remain part of reviewed delivery."
  "2026-10-20T16:26:33.092Z","harness:codex","Review remediation: use the plain rendered retry example for Windows and POSIX portability, keep bounded-wait policy in required guidance, and update the older malformed-vector test to reject the whole vector while retaining a valid padded/empty-token control. CodeRabbit's TTL documentation finding is accepted: an unexpired live or unknown owner stays protected, while expiration retains the existing removal policy. Related sibling recovery and release/dependency census references now have real typed relationships rather than raising graph limits."
  "2026-10-20T16:56:33.818Z","harness:codex","Final implementation evidence:197 focused review tests and both linked commands pass, plus all required checks on d89ad584c. Hosted complete coverage is exact100/100/100/100 with10846 passing and3 skipped cases. All four accepted inline findings are fixed and resolved; final full review awaits the next included free slot. CLI-only tracker mutations refreshed release actual results and the single October21 06:00UTC reminder. Generated changelog and terminal closure will be reviewed in this same PR."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T16:56:31.362Z","harness:codex","Executable recovery arguments are opaque values: retain whitespace and empty strings, and omit malformed vectors rather than deleting tokens. Keep wait policy separate from rendered commands so retry examples remain portable."
